        "subject": "feat: Vercel Speed Insights + Web Analytics (#194)",
        "body": "feat: Vercel Speed Insights + Web Analytics (#194)\n\n* feat: add Vercel Speed Insights and Web Analytics\n\nAdd <SpeedInsights /> and <Analytics /> to the root layout per Vercel's\nApp Router quickstart. Enables the Speed Insights and Analytics dashboards\nfor the deployed app.\n\nAdds .npmrc legacy-peer-deps=true: @vercel/analytics declares an optional\n@sveltejs/kit peer that drags in a Svelte->Vite 8 chain conflicting with the\nproject's Vite 7; nothing Svelte is used. The flag keeps npm install and CI's\nnpm ci from failing on that spurious conflict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: declare vite + @testing-library/dom explicitly for legacy-peer-deps\n\nlegacy-peer-deps (added for @vercel/analytics) reverts npm to npm-6 behaviour\nand stops auto-installing peer deps. Two peers the project relied on then\nvanished from a clean 'npm ci':\n- vite (peer of @vitejs/plugin-react, loaded by vitest.config.mts)\n- @testing-library/dom (peer of @testing-library/react, used by .test.tsx)\n\nDeclare both as explicit devDependencies. Verified with a clean\n'rm -rf node_modules && npm ci' + lint + test:ci + build (CI parity).\nnpm ls confirms these were the only non-optional unmet peers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
